            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Motivated by questions in biology, we investigate the stability of equilibria of the dynamical system [Formula: see text] which arise as critical points of f, under the assumption that [Formula: see text] is positive semi-definite. It is shown that the condition [Formula: see text], where [Formula: see text] is the smallest eigenvalue of [Formula: see text], plays a key role in guaranteeing uniform asymptotic stability and in providing information on the basis of attraction of those equilibria.</AbstractText>
